      "hints": [
        "Differentiate $y = x^2 - 2x - 3$ to find $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2x - 2$.",
        "Use the chain rule $\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{dy/dt}{dx/dt} = \\frac{4}{6} = \\frac{2}{3}$.",
        "Solve $2x - 2 = \\frac{2}{3}$ for $x$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate the curve equation with respect to $x$:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2x - 2$$",
        "Apply the chain rule for connected rates of change:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{\\frac{dy}{dt}}{\\frac{dx}{dt}} = \\frac{4}{6} = \\frac{2}{3}$$",
        "Equate the two expressions for the gradient and solve for $x$:\n$$2x - 2 = \\frac{2}{3} \\implies 2x = 2 + \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{8}{3} \\implies x = \\frac{4}{3} \\quad \\left(\\text{or } 1\\frac{1}{3}\\right)$$"
      ],
